## Authority boundaries

- Program Beads are the sole live authority for cross-repository work. Source
  repositories retain their local implementation tasks.
- `ROADMAP.md` defines durable gates; it never mirrors Beads status.
- Dated ADRs record accepted decisions; they do not track implementation state.
- Registry YAML records approved immutable identities and pointers. A correction
  receives a new ID with `supersedes`; a registered file is never edited.
- Producer and consumer repositories own all computation. This repository
  approves contracts and compatibility records but never launches their jobs.

## Hard boundaries

No Git submodules, sibling source imports, pipeline launchers, scientific
environments, notebooks, containers, acquired/derived data, model checkpoints,
latent arrays, figures, or reports belong here. Registry records use durable
URIs and full SHA-256 digests; they never use a workstation path or credential.

